 steps:['现象','原因','影响','建议','结论'],
 model:['The workplace is changing faster than at any time in the past century. Automation, remote work and shifting employee expectations are reshaping how organizations operate.','Technology is the most visible driver. Routine tasks are increasingly performed by machines, while demand grows for skills such as creativity, communication and critical thinking.','These changes bring opportunities but also risks. Workers who cannot adapt may be left behind, and the boundary between work and private life may blur.','Governments and employers should invest in lifelong learning, and individuals should take responsibility for updating their skills.','The future of work is not something that simply happens to us; it is something we can shape.'],
